<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.14.2: Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01500</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.14.2: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4ece93cc-87f5-4bcd-a60f-d1fa9ee838a9</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Using a calculator, Joanna made the following table and then made the following conjecture: \(3x\) is always greater than \((1.02)^x\). Is Joanna correct? Explain.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        \(x\)
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        \((1.02)^x\)
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        \(3x\)
      </entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1.02
      </entry>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1.0404
      </entry>
      <entry>
        6
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1.0612
      </entry>
      <entry>
        9
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        4
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1.0824
      </entry>
      <entry>
        12
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        5
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1.1041
      </entry>
      <entry>
        15
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
</section>
</content>
</document>
